<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="fo6" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>FO6: Slope Fields</title>
    <objectives>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <p>
                    I can use a slope field to analyze the behaviors of solutions to a differential equation.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </objectives>
    
    <definition xml:id="def-slope-field">
        <title>Slope Field</title>
        <idx><h>slope field</h></idx>
        <statement>
            <p>
                For a differential equation of the form <m>y' = f(x,y)</m>, its <term>slope field</term> is the collection of lines of slopes to solution curves at various points in the plane.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </definition>

    <example>
        <statement>
            <p>
                The slope field for the differential equation <m>\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 3x^2-5</m> is given below, along with three solution curves.
            </p>
            <figure xml:id="fo6-slopegraph-1">
                <image width="60%">
                    <xi:include href="img/fo6-slopegraph-1.xml"/>
                </image>
                <caption>The slope field of <m>y' = 3x^2-5</m>, along with three solutions</caption>
            </figure>
            <p>
                This is separable, and we get the family of solutions <m>y = x^3 -5x + C</m>, which aligns well with the images in the graph above. The different curves drawn correspond to different initial values of the function. 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </example>

    <example>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Slope fields can be used to analyze the qualitative behavior of solutions to functions. Take for example the differential equation
                <md>
                    \dfrac{dy}{dt} = t - y^2 
                </md>
                This is neither linear nor separable, so we can't solve it using any known techniques. The slope field can help us determine the long-term behavior of the ODE.
            </p>
            <figure xml:id="fo6-slopegraph-2">
                <image width="60%">
                    <xi:include href="img/fo6-slopegraph-2.xml"/>
                </image>
                <caption>The slope field of <m>y' = t-y^2</m></caption>
            </figure>
        </statement>
    </example>

    <exercise>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Below is the slope field for the differential equation <m>x' + 2tx = x</m>. 
            </p>
            <figure xml:id="fo6-slopegraph-3">
                <image width="60%">
                    <xi:include href="img/fo6-slopegraph-3.xml"/>
                </image>
                <caption>The slope field of <m>x' + 2tx = x</m>.</caption>
            </figure>
            <p>
                <ol marker="a.">
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Describe the behavior of the solution when <m>x(0) = 5</m>.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            The equation is separable. Determine the solution and compare the behaviors.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

</section>